    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThey were considered, but they have shortcomings which I find significant:\r\n- I would like users to be able to remove plugins by just deleting its directory. The reason is that usually plugin-to-be-removed is obsolete and not used, so removing from outside of Neovim doesn't make much sense to me.\r\n- In order for those hooks to be called, plugin should be loaded. So to remove plugin user should first load it with proper hooks. As, again, plugin-to-be-removed is usually obsolete and not loaded to begin with, it makes the whole approach quite unintuitive to me.\r\n\r\nI am afraid this won't be added. Unless, probably, the upstream (Neovim) finalizes the packspec which *will* include those hooks.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">They were considered, but they have shortcomings which I find significant:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I would like users to be able to remove plugins by just deleting its directory. The reason is that usually plugin-to-be-removed is obsolete and not used, so removing from outside of Neovim doesn't make much sense to me.</li>\n<li>In order for those hooks to be called, plugin should be loaded. So to remove plugin user should first load it with proper hooks. As, again, plugin-to-be-removed is usually obsolete and not loaded to begin with, it makes the whole approach quite unintuitive to me.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid this won't be added. Unless, probably, the upstream (Neovim) finalizes the packspec which <em>will</em> include those hooks.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for the suggestion!\nThey were considered, but they have shortcomings which I find significant:\n\nI would like users to be able to remove plugins by just deleting its directory. The reason is that usually plugin-to-be-removed is obsolete and not used, so removing from outside of Neovim doesn't make much sense to me.\nIn order for those hooks to be called, plugin should be loaded. So to remove plugin user should first load it with proper hooks. As, again, plugin-to-be-removed is usually obsolete and not loaded to begin with, it makes the whole approach quite unintuitive to me.\n\nI am afraid this won't be added. Unless, probably, the upstream (Neovim) finalizes the packspec which will include those hooks.",
